[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/2679474117","html_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono/issues/3952#issuecomment-2679474117","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/3952","id":2679474117,"node_id":"IC_kwDOGiE5WM6ftYfF","user":{"login":"lincolnremi","id":177562579,"node_id":"U_kgDOCpVj0w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177562579?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lincolnremi","html_url":"https://github.com/lincolnremi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lincolnremi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lincolnremi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lincolnremi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lincolnremi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lincolnremi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lincolnremi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lincolnremi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lincolnremi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lincolnremi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-24T19:39:58Z","updated_at":"2025-02-24T19:39:58Z","body":"This patch should work:\n\n```\ndiff --git a/src/middleware/pretty-json/index.ts b/src/middleware/pretty-json/index.ts\nindex bc198e58..a5428f7d 100644\n--- a/src/middleware/pretty-json/index.ts\n+++ b/src/middleware/pretty-json/index.ts\n@@ -40,7 +40,15 @@ interface PrettyOptions {\n export const prettyJSON = (options?: PrettyOptions): MiddlewareHandler => {\n   const targetQuery = options?.query ?? 'pretty'\n   return async function prettyJSON(c, next) {\n-    const pretty = c.req.query(targetQuery) || c.req.query(targetQuery) === ''\n+    let pretty;\n+    try {\n+      pretty = c.req.query(targetQuery) || c.req.query(targetQuery) === ''\n+    } catch (e) {\n+      // Ignore URIError caused by invalid query parameter\n+      if (!(e instanceof URIError)) {\n+        throw e;\n+      }\n+    }\n     await next()\n     if (pretty && c.res.headers.get('Content-Type')?.startsWith('application/json')) {\n       const obj = await c.res.json()\n```\n\nI can put this into a PR & test if the maintainers are open to it","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/2679474117/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/2692607026","html_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono/issues/3952#issuecomment-2692607026","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/3952","id":2692607026,"node_id":"IC_kwDOGiE5WM6gfewy","user":{"login":"yusukebe","id":10682,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNjgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10682?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe","html_url":"https://github.com/yusukebe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-02T07:49:46Z","updated_at":"2025-03-02T07:49:46Z","body":"Hi @lincolnremi Thank you for the issue! Good catch. But please wait a bit.\n\nHey @usualoma ! What do you think of the following?\n\nNot only a Pretty JSON middleware case, but I wonder whether it is correct behavior to get a `URIError: URI malformed` error if you passed an invalid query to `c.req.query()`.\n\nIn the case of Express, instead of throwing an error, the invalid query is treated as a string.\n\nThe app code:\n\n```js\nconst express = require('express')\nconst app = express()\n\napp.get('/', (req, res) => {\n  const foo = req.query.foo\n  res.send(`foo: ${foo}`)\n})\n\napp.listen(3000, () => {\n  console.log('Server is running on port 3000')\n})\n```\n\nThe results:\n\n```txt\n$ curl 'localhost:3000?foo=%E3%81%82'\nfoo: あ%\n$ curl 'localhost:3000?foo=%E3%81%8'\nfoo: %E3%81%8%\n```\n\nBut the Hono app:\n\n```ts\nimport { Hono } from 'hono'\n\nconst app = new Hono()\n\napp.get('/', (c) => {\n  const foo = c.req.query('foo')\n  return c.text(`foo: ${foo}`)\n})\n\nexport default app\n```\n\nPerhaps we should follow the same spec as Express?\nThe results:\n\n```txt\n$ curl 'localhost:3000?foo=%E3%81%82'\nfoo: あ%\n$ curl 'localhost:3000?foo=%E3%81%8'\nInternal Server Error%\n```\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/2692607026/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/2692650008","html_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono/issues/3952#issuecomment-2692650008","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/3952","id":2692650008,"node_id":"IC_kwDOGiE5WM6gfpQY","user":{"login":"EdamAme-x","id":121654029,"node_id":"U_kgDOB0BLDQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121654029?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdamAme-x","html_url":"https://github.com/EdamAme-x","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdamAme-x/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdamAme-x/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdamAme-x/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdamAme-x/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdamAme-x/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdamAme-x/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdamAme-x/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdamAme-x/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdamAme-x/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-02T09:49:28Z","updated_at":"2025-03-02T09:50:02Z","body":"*Express* relies on query parser libraries such as *qs*.\nAs suggested by someone before, it might be a good idea to add a custom query parser option.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/2692650008/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/2692714718","html_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono/issues/3952#issuecomment-2692714718","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/3952","id":2692714718,"node_id":"IC_kwDOGiE5WM6gf5De","user":{"login":"usualoma","id":30598,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNTk4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30598?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/usualoma","html_url":"https://github.com/usualoma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/usualoma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/usualoma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/usualoma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/usualoma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/usualoma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/usualoma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/usualoma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/usualoma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/usualoma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-02T12:44:46Z","updated_at":"2025-03-02T12:44:46Z","body":"I also think it would be good if the result here was the same as with the express.\n\n```bash\n$ curl 'localhost:3000?foo=%E3%81%82'\nfoo: あ\n$ curl 'localhost:3000?foo=%E3%81%8'\nfoo: %E3%81%8\n```\n\nI think it would be better if users defined and used their own custom query parser. I think it is more likely that users want to use their own parser because they want to define their own type, so I think it would be better if they defined it themselves rather than incorporating it into the hono.\n\n```ts\nconst foo = new myCustomQuery(c).get(‘foo’)\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/2692714718/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/2692918038","html_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono/issues/3952#issuecomment-2692918038","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/3952","id":2692918038,"node_id":"IC_kwDOGiE5WM6ggqsW","user":{"login":"yusukebe","id":10682,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNjgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10682?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe","html_url":"https://github.com/yusukebe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-02T21:31:54Z","updated_at":"2025-03-02T21:31:54Z","body":"@EdamAme-x @usualoma \n\nThank you for the comments!\n\nRegarding the custom query parser, I prefer to use the syntax @usualoma suggested.\n\n```ts\nmyCustomQuery(c).get(‘foo’)\n```\n\nBut we should discuss implementing the same behavior with Express for the default. Of course, the user can change the behavior with the custom query parser, but almost all users do not use it, and the default behavior is important.\n\nWe can treat the difference between Hono's and Express's as a bug or unexpected behavior. I think we should make it so that the error is not thrown if `c.req.query` parses invalid strings since it can cause vulnerability by intentionally sending invalid values. It's unexpected behavior, so I think it would be better that we should fix it.\n\nI want to know what you think.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/2692918038/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/2745203982","html_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono/issues/3952#issuecomment-2745203982","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/3952","id":2745203982,"node_id":"IC_kwDOGiE5WM6joH0O","user":{"login":"usualoma","id":30598,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNTk4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30598?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/usualoma","html_url":"https://github.com/usualoma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/usualoma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/usualoma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/usualoma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/usualoma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/usualoma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/usualoma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/usualoma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/usualoma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/usualoma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-22T10:35:10Z","updated_at":"2025-03-22T10:35:10Z","body":"Hi @yusukebe. I'm sorry for not getting back to you sooner.\n\nYes, I also think it would be preferable to make it behave the same as Express. I believe the following changes would achieve this.\n\n```diff\ndiff --git a/src/utils/url.ts b/src/utils/url.ts\nindex 27604022..5772adae 100644\n--- a/src/utils/url.ts\n+++ b/src/utils/url.ts\n@@ -216,7 +216,7 @@ const _decodeURI = (value: string) => {\n   if (value.indexOf('+') !== -1) {\n     value = value.replace(/\\+/g, ' ')\n   }\n-  return value.indexOf('%') !== -1 ? decodeURIComponent_(value) : value\n+  return value.indexOf('%') !== -1 ? tryDecode(value, decodeURIComponent_) : value\n }\n \n const _getQueryParam = (\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/2745203982/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/2987208264","html_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono/issues/3952#issuecomment-2987208264","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/3952","id":2987208264,"node_id":"IC_kwDOGiE5WM6yDS5I","user":{"login":"yusukebe","id":10682,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNjgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10682?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe","html_url":"https://github.com/yusukebe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-19T08:31:21Z","updated_at":"2025-06-19T08:31:21Z","body":"This issue was fixed with #4110. You can use the latest version `4.8.0` including the fix! Thanks.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/2987208264/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]